    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18125" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφά̆ν-εια</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>obscurity, uncertainty,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τύχας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>I.</u>
					4(3).49
				</span></i>
			: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀξιώματος ἀ.</span>
			<i>want of illustrious</i> birth or rank, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.37
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>invisibility,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Dam.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				6
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>disappearance, destruction,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				384
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Procl.
				<u>in Prm.</u>
				p.840S.
			</span></i>—The form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφανία</span></b>  is mentioned by <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Synt.</u>
				341.8
			</span></i>.</div>
